(A function parameter that shadows a top-level variable must not
 relabel it for the code after the definition - the text/buffer
 labels stay scoped to the function body)
a number called "x" is 5.
a number called "b" is 7.

To "show" with a text called "x" and a buffer called "b",
  Print x.

Print x add 1.
Print b add 1.
